      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the standard first-line medication for type 2 diabetes, but SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are increasingly prioritized early or alongside metformin based on individual organ protection goals.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are increasingly prioritized early or alongside metformin based on individual organ protection goals"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Core Differences"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors (e.g., ): Oral pills taken once daily. They excel at protecting the kidneys and managing or preventing heart failure. They lower A1C by about 0.5% to 1% and cause modest weight loss. Common side effects include genital and urinary tract infections.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "link": "https://patient.boehringer-ingelheim.com/us/products/jardiance/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "GLP-1 Receptor Agonists (e.g., Ozempic): Mostly weekly injections, though some oral options exist. They excel at lowering blood sugar (reducing A1C by up to 1.5% to 2%) and promoting substantial weight loss. They also lower the risk of major cardiovascular events like stroke. Common side effects are gastrointestinal, such as nausea and vomiting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Choosing Based on Comorbidities"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Clinical guidelines from groups like the American Diabetes Association recommend choosing between the two classes depending on specific health conditions:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose an SGLT2 inhibitor first if: You have a history of heart failure or chronic kidney disease."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose a GLP-1 receptor agonist first if: Your primary goals are significant weight loss, reducing obesity-related cardiometabolic risk, or lowering atherosclerotic cardiovascular risk (like stroke prevention)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down which option might fit your situation, please share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have any underlying heart or kidney conditions ?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Is weight loss a primary treatment goal for you?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have a strong preference between an oral pill or an ?"
          }
        ]
      }
